Package: pannet
Type: Package
Title: Neural Regression for Panel Data with Nonlinear Covariate Effects
Version: 0.7.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Imad", family = "El Badisy", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "elbadisyimad@gmail.com")
Description: Fits panel and longitudinal regression models with a multilayer
    perceptron in place of the linear index used by classical fixed- and
    random-effects estimators, while keeping additive learnable individual
    and time effects a plain neural network would otherwise drop. Intended
    for panels where the covariate-response relationship is genuinely
    nonlinear: validated across independent simulation replications to
    recover such effects substantially better than a linear panel
    estimator, and competitively with a correctly-specified additive
    panel model without requiring the functional form to be named in
    advance (see the package vignettes). Supports Gaussian, binomial, Poisson,
    multiclass, and fractional outcomes, with pooled, individual-effect,
    time-effect, two-way-effect, and dynamic (lagged) panel structures.
    Training is performed natively via the 'torch' package with no external
    learner dependency.
